","years":[2009]},{"country_code":"TH","id":"I48076826","name":"Chiang Mai University","years":[2006]},{"country_code":"US","id":"I161203489","name":"Youngstown State University","years":[2006]},{"country_code":"CA","id":"I154425047","name":"University of Alberta","years":[2002]},{"country_code":"US","id":"I1339417872","name":"Wadsworth Center","years":[2002]},{"country_code":"VE","id":"I191242182","name":"Instituto Venezolano de Investigaciones Cient\u00edficas","years":[2001]},{"country_code":"US","id":"I188871143","name":"Saint Vincent College","years":[2001]},{"country_code":"MX","id":"I81992734","name":"Universidad del Valle de M\u00e9xico","years":[2001]},{"country_code":"GB","id":"I98677209","name":"University of Edinburgh","years":[1996,1998,2000]},{"country_code":"US","id":"I97018004","name":"Stanford University","years":[1999]}],"author_id":"A5065133902","ca_plastic_works_count":1,"ca_works_count":1,"citations_by_year":[{"all":1533,"plastic":0,"year":2017},{"all":1535,"plastic":0,"year":2018},{"all":1937,"plastic":0,"year":2019},{"all":2344,"plastic":0,"year":2020},{"all":2799,"plastic":1,"year":2021},{"all":2423,"plastic":6,"year":2022},{"all":2773,"plastic":8,"year":2023},{"all":3001,"plastic":16,"year":2024},{"all":3002,"plastic":18,"year":2025},{"all":2716,"plastic":19,"year":2026}],"cited_by_count":31876,"domain_tags":[],"early_career":false,"first_pub_year":1993,"first_year":2026,"h_index":78,"institution_ids":["I1344073410","I95457486"],"last_year":2026,"m_quotient":2.36,"name":"Matthew C. Fisher","orcid":"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1862-6402","plastic_basis":"openalex","plastic_citations":68,"plastic_works_count":3,"primary_affiliations":[{"country_code":"US","id":"I1344073410","name":"Howard Hughes Medical Institute","source":"openalex_last_known"},{"country_code":"GB","id":"I47508984","name":"Imperial College London","source":"openalex_last_known"},{"country_code":"GB","id":"I90344618","name":"Medical Research Council","source":"openalex_last_known"},{"country_code":"US","id":"I95457486","name":"University of California, Berkeley","source":"openalex_last_known"}],"rising_pct":64,"rising_score":0.0039,"work_count":1,"work_ids":["W7135184874"]},"profile":{"bio":"Prof Matthew Fisher is a biologist with a focus on the biodiversity and evolutionary ecology of pathogenic fungi. He heads the Fungal Pathogens Research Group in the Department of Infectious Disease Epidemiology and leads the Fungal Pathogens theme in the MRC Centre for Global Infectious Disease Analysis. His research uses evolutionary genomics, molecular taxonomy, field ecology and experimentation to investigate the biological and environmental factors that are driving emerging fungal diseases across managed and natural ecosystems. His lab works across scales ranging from single-hosts\u2026","keywords":["Fungal biology","Infectious Disease Epidemiology"],"links":[{"label":"Matthew Fisher webpage","url":"https://profiles.imperial.ac.uk/matthew.fisher"}]},"schema_version":"s3.1","works":[{"abstract":"Abstract Candida ( Candidozyma ) auris is a critical priority fungal pathogen that emerged two decades ago near simultaneously on multiple continents. Since emergence, C. auris resistance to all four classes of antifungal drugs has been described, including pan-drug resistant isolates, sometimes evolving within patients. Here, we confirm the first isolation of C. auris from Antarctica and show cold-adapted phenotypes and an affinity for binding to nylon. We also provide evidence to suggest mutator phenotypes contribute to the rapid evolution of C. auris and are responsible for the emergence of multiple, distinct genetic clades worldwide. Isolates in clades I, III and IV with a mutator phenotype displayed elevated mutation rates compared to non- auris Candida species. This phenotype had a complex genetic basis and was associated with drug resistance mutations. We postulate that the mutator phenotype has a significant effect on evolutionary potential and is responsible for the emergence and rapid spread of drug-resistance C. auris and novel genetic clades.","author_ids":["A5009421399","A5026173669","A5032906326","A5038725561","A5039990140","A5047875566","A5050234766","A5062892359","A5065133902","A5070474104","A5071152958","A5076265294","A5080533196","A5112793452","A5124069266","A5129039551","A5129060437","A5129060625","A5129063258"],"author_institution_ids":["I1344073410","I95457486"],"ca_any_author":true,"ca_led":false,"cited_by_count":3,"doi":"https://doi.org/10.64898/2026.03.13.711634","domain_tags":[],"facet_tags":["matrix:marine"],"institution_ids":["I1344073410","I23923803","I27804330","I28407311","I3018483916","I4387153084","I4387153154","I47508984","I79619799","I95457486"],"is_oa":true,"journal":"bioRxiv (Cold Spring Harbor Laboratory)","last_updated":"2026-11-11T12:16:26.678958","license":"cc-by-nd","needs_review":false,"oa_status":"green","oa_url":"https://www.biorxiv.org/content/biorxiv/early/2026/03/13/2026.03.13.711634.full.pdf","openalex_topics":["T10150","T10753","T12668"],"plastic_related":true,"plastic_tier":"core","primary_topic":"T10150","pub_date":"2026-03-13","study_type":"preprint","title":"Antarctic marine microplastics reveals environmental persistence and rapid evolution of Candida auris","type":"preprint","work_id":"W7135184874","year":2026}]}
